 --border:#3a3a37;--text:#fff;--text-2:#c3c2b7;--text-3:#96958c}
body{margin:0;background:var(--surface);color:var(--text);
 font:15px/1.55 ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",system-ui,sans-serif}
.wrap{max-width:1500px;margin:0 auto;padding:32px 24px 72px}
h1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 4px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
h2{font-size:1.05rem;margin:40px 0 10px;letter-spacing:-.005em}
.sub{color:var(--text-2);font-size:.9rem;margin:0 0 24px}
.tiles{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(160px,1fr));gap:12px;margin:20px 0 8px}
.tile{background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px}
.tile .v{font-size:1.7rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.tile .k{color:var(--text-2);font-size:.78rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;margin-top:2px}
.tile .d{color:var(--text-3);font-size:.75rem;margin-top:4px}
.note{background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:3px solid var(--warning);
 border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;color:var(--text-2);font-size:.85rem;margin:18px 0}
.note.method{border-left-color:var(--neutral)}
.scroll{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;margin-top:8px}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.86rem}
th,td{text-align:left;padding:8px 11px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);white-space:nowrap}
th{background:var(--surface-2);position:sticky;top:0;cursor:pointer;user-select:none;
 font-weight:600;font-size:.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--text-2)}
th:hover{color:var(--text)}
th[data-dir]::after{content:"";margin-left:5px}
th[data-dir="1"]::after{content:"\2191"}
th[data-dir="-1"]::after{content:"\2193"}
tbody tr:hover{background:var(--surface-2)}
td.num,th.num{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
th.num{font-variant-numeric:normal}
.pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-size:.76rem;font-weight:600;
 padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid currentColor}
.pill.critical{color:var(--critical)}.pill.serious{color:var(--serious)}
.pill.warning{color:var(--warning)}.pill.neutral{color:var(--neutral)}
.tag{display:inline-block;font-size:.72rem;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;
 background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-2);margin-right:4px}
.reason{color:var(--text-2);font-size:.8rem;white-space:normal;min-width:280px}
.empty{color:var(--text-2);padding:14px 2px;font-size:.9rem}
footer{margin-top:48px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);
 color:var(--text-3);font-size:.78rem}
code{font-size:.85em;background:var(--surface-2);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px}

.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:14px;
 margin:22px 0}
.card{background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;
 padding:18px 20px;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;display:block;transition:border-color .15s}
.card:hover{border-color:var(--text-3)}
.card h2{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:1.05rem}
.card p{margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--text-2);font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.5}
.card .meta{color:var(--text-3);font-size:.76rem}
.card.missing{opacity:.55;cursor:default}
.card.missing .meta{color:var(--warning)}
.q{color:var(--text-2);font-size:.87rem;margin:4px 0 0}
</style></head><body><div class="wrap">
<h1>Healthcare credit</h1>
<p class="sub">Bond, loan and provider-financial coverage A� generated 2026-11-16 12:32 UTC</p>


<div class="cards"><a class="card" href="hospital_distress_latest.html"><h2>Hospital &amp; SNF distress census</h2><p>Are more providers losing money than in the past? Every Medicare-participating hospital and skilled-nursing facility, FY2016 onward �?" the full census, no survivorship bias.</p><div class="meta">updated 2026-11-16 12:32 UTC A� 16 KB</div></a><a class="card" href="bond_screen_latest.html"><h2>Credit screen �?" what is cheap</h2><p>Healthcare debt trading wide of its own market: distressed and stressed tiers, quarter-over-quarter widening, and where funds disagree on the same bond's mark.</p><div class="meta">updated 2026-11-16 12:32 UTC A� 1,059 KB</div></a><a class="card" href="coverage_bonds_latest.html"><h2>Coverage universe �?" bonds &amp; loans</h2><p>Every instrument your coverage names have outstanding, with yield, spread and maturity, plus sub-sector medians on your own equity taxonomy.</p><div class="meta">updated 2026-11-16 12:32 UTC A� 535 KB</div></a><a class="card" href="capital_structure_latest.html"><h2>Capital structure by company</h2><p>Every bond and loan one borrower has outstanding, ordered by maturity, with the fund's own fair-value level per instrument �?" the view that sits next to an equity position.</p><div class="meta">updated 2026-11-16 12:32 UTC A� 513 KB</div></a><a class="card" href="balance_sheet_debt_latest.html"><h2>Balance-sheet debt &mdash; who owes what</h2><p>Long-term debt for every coverage name from its own XBRL filings &mdash; including the revolver-financed borrowers (Ensign, Chemed, Addus, PACS) that no fund holds and every other page is structurally blind to. Par owed, not market value.</p><div class="meta">updated 2026-11-16 12:32 UTC A� 79 KB</div></a><a class="card" href="healthcare_loans_latest.html"><h2>Healthcare leveraged loans</h2><p>The loan market, quoted on discount margin �?" including the private borrowers (Waystar, athenahealth, Radiology Partners) that have no listed equity and appear nowhere else.</p><div class="meta">updated 2026-11-16 12:32 UTC A� 41 KB</div></a></div>

<div class="note method"><strong>How the pieces fit.</strong> Two independent evidence bases,
because neither can substitute for the other. The <strong>bond and loan pages</strong> price
individual instruments from fund holdings filings �?" but they only ever see debt some fund
still owns, which is a self-selected slice that omits exactly the credits a manager has
already sold. The <strong>census</strong> covers every provider from cost reports, so it can
say whether the sector is deteriorating at all. Individual distressed credits mean something
quite different depending on which way the census is pointing.</div>

<div class="note"><strong>Freshness.</strong> Bond and loan marks come from quarterly holdings
filings and run roughly 60 days in arrears �?" they show where a bond <em>is</em>, not where you
could deal. Cost reports refresh quarterly and are re-pulled automatically when they go stale.
Everything regenerates Monday mornings; new debt filings are scanned weekly and posted to
<strong>#credit</strong>.</div>

<footer>Generated by <code>bond_credit</code>. Sources: SEC EDGAR (NPORT-P holdings, 8-K,
424B5/FWP), FRED (Treasury curve, ICE BofA index OAS, SOFR), CMS HCRIS cost reports.</footer>
</div></body></html>
