  89: 
  90: <div class="note method"><strong>What is measured.</strong> Total margin = net income A� total
  91: revenue, taken from Worksheet G-3 of each hospital's cost report. This is the all-in figure
  92: and is comparable to published benchmarks. It is <em>not</em> the "operating margin" Kaufman
  93: Hall and the AHA report �?" that excludes non-operating income and would not match. Every
  94: hospital is counted once per fiscal year, using its most complete filing, and years are the
  95: cost report's own fiscal year, which is staggered across the calendar rather than aligned to
  96: it.</div>
  97: 
  98: <div class="note"><strong>Why this exists alongside the bond screen.</strong> The bond panel
  99: only ever sees hospitals whose debt some fund still holds �?" a small and self-selected slice
 100: that omits exactly the credits a fund has already sold. This is the whole census, from an
 101: entirely separate source, so the two agreeing is corroboration rather than an echo.</div>
 102: 
 103: <div class="note"><strong>Excluded as incomplete:</strong> FY2014 (18), FY2015 (3,404), FY2026 (280). CMS names each archive for its <em>processing</em> year, not the fiscal years inside it, so the newest and oldest years of any ingest hold only part of the census. Charting them beside complete years would show a cliff that is an artefact of ingestion rather than anything about hospitals.</div>
