  58:       <p><b>Heat scale</b> �?" diverging around zero, fixed rather than percentile-ranked:
  59:       <span class="chip" style="background:#F0C7C3"></span> (10%) &nbsp;<span class="chip" style="background:#F0EFEC"></span> 0% &nbsp;<span class="chip" style="background:#FFEB9C"></span> 5% &nbsp;<span class="chip" style="background:#B7DE98"></span> 12% &nbsp;<span class="chip" style="background:#63BE7B"></span> 25% &nbsp;<br>Red is contraction, neutral gray is flat, green is growth. Lightness falls
  60:       steadily along each arm, so magnitude is legible from lightness alone, and every
  61:       negative is additionally written in parentheses �?" so the sign survives for readers who
  62:       cannot separate red from green, without the colour itself having to carry it.</p>
  63:       <p><b>A�</b> marks a cell whose row has no data source yet �?" <b>5</b>
  64:       rows are awaiting an <code>earnings_kpi</code>
  65:       extraction fan-out, and <b>5</b>
  66:       rows resolved a source but produced no YoY pair in range,
  67:       and <b>0</b> rows have a working source whose
  68:       history does not yet reach back a full year, so no YoY can be formed.
  69:       Rows marked <i>interim</i> are consolidated revenue standing in for a same-facility
