  89:            marker's rule is `td.marker`, which a span cannot match and a nested table would
  90:            only satisfy by putting a table inside a <p> �?" invalid, and the browser silently
  91:            closes the paragraph around it. So the sample carries the rule inline instead. -->
  92:       <p><b>Cell markers</b> �?"
  93:       <span style="color:#b08900;font-size:10px">&ne;</span>
  94:       <b>withheld</b>: the two periods are not like-for-like, so no growth rate is published
  95:       (hover for the reason) &middot;
  96:       <sup class="cw">&#9888;</sup> <b>rendered, with a caveat</b> �?" hover for it: either the
  97:       period is offset from the calendar quarter it sits in, or the comparison window moved
  98:       (same length, displaced) &middot;
  99:       <span class="basis">~</span> period dates assumed, so comparability could not be checked
 100:       &middot; <span class="derived">&Delta;</span> computed from two published rows rather
 101:       than reported directly &middot; <span class="star">*</span> on a row label, the fiscal
 102:       period is offset from the calendar quarter; in a Period-average header, the year is
 103:       partial.</p>
 104:       <p><b>Period average</b> block on the right averages a row's ACTUAL quarters only �?"
 105:       an estimates column is not a period anyone has reported. A year marked
 106:       <span class="star">*</span> in that header is partial: fewer than four quarters of it
 107:       are on the sheet, so its average is not a full year. The solid rule falls after each
